## Wire Bootstrap

- `rishadblack/wire-bootstrap` provides Livewire-native Bootstrap 5.3 UI: `php artisan wire-bootstrap:install` sets up Bootstrap, SCSS, Vite and a base layout in one command, and every form field is a single Blade tag. Activate the `wire-bootstrap-development` skill whenever you build forms or pages with `<x-wire-bootstrap::*>` / `<x-wb::*>` components, run the installer, or add a new field component.
- A field is one tag: `<x-wb::input.text label="Name" wire:model="name" required />` renders the label with a required marker, derives `id`/`name` from `wire:model`, shows the validation error (`is-invalid` + `invalid-feedback`) and defaults the placeholder from the label. Never hand-write Bootstrap form groups for things these components cover.
- Fields: `input.text|email|number|hidden|password|textarea|select|select-search|checkbox|switch|checkbox-group|radio|date|file|color|range`. UI: `button`, `card`, `tabs`/`tab`, `badge`, `alert`, `empty-state`, `theme-toggle`, `layout`. Common props: `label`, `name`, `id`, `placeholder` (`""` suppresses), `required`, `optional`, `help`, `size`, `floating`, `wrapper-class`, `prepend`/`append`. Other attributes pass through to the control.
- Fields render `aria-required`, never the native `required` attribute, so Livewire's server-side validation always runs — validate in the component.
- `input.select`, `input.radio` and `input.checkbox-group` take `:options` as `['key' => 'Label']` or `[['value' => 1, 'name' => 'Label']]`; a slot of `<option>` tags wins over `:options`.
- `<x-wb::button type="submit" loading="save">` (or any `wire:click`) disables itself and shows a spinner while the action runs. Variants via `variant`/`outline`/`size`, never separate per-color components.
- `input.date` wraps flatpickr behind `wire:ignore`; accepted date spellings are `Y-m-d`, `d-M-Y`, `d-m-Y` or `strtotime` input, and `$this->dispatch('wire-bootstrap:date-options', model: ..., enable: [...])` updates enabled dates at runtime.
- Behaviour is Bootstrap `data-bs-*` attributes + Alpine only. Do not add jQuery, loose `<script>` blocks or DOM listeners outside Alpine; new interactivity belongs in an Alpine component in the package JS.
- When `livewire/blaze` is installed the package auto-opts its views into Blaze's function compiler (config `wire-bootstrap.blaze`). Package components stay anonymous components with a full `@props` contract — never read `$attributes['foo']` for a prop, and keep logic in `Rishadblack\WireBootstrap\Support\*` (`FieldState::resolve()` + `<x-wire-bootstrap::field>` for new fields).
- Views never reference CDNs or push `<style>` blocks; assets come from the installer-managed `resources/scss/app.scss` and `resources/js/wire-bootstrap-setup.js`. Theme with SCSS variable overrides, published lang lines (`wire-bootstrap-lang`) or published views (`wire-bootstrap-views`).
